ascot from a local theme park starts suspiciously, repeatedly bringing in children with broken arms for treatment. The hospital is turned into a youth hostel, and Sy gets conned by an attractive young foreign girl.","poster":"e2852b8b43fe83a9244add39b1b2ca50","premiere":"2010-09-12T00:00:00.0000000Z","season":2,"seasonId":"a1dd04d3de83387876e8861ed26bc69b","secs":676,"series":"Childrens Hospital","seriesId":"374db935fd4f66d27bd999d10d592bcd","tags":{"backdrop":"0f5076b938df","poster":"75a2d5d3b358"},"type":"episode","year":2010},{"added":"2024-04-15T12:58:18.0000000Z","backdrop":"374db935fd4f66d27bd999d10d592bcd","ep":5,"id":"4d67b66325e518fae3183b8b24364994","mins":11,"name":"Joke Overload","overview":"The staff must choose between saving an old black man and a young white kid. Insult comic Jeffrey Ross brings his child into the O.R., but the staff is more concerned with enjoying his humor than treating his child. Two Star Trek nerds dressed in uniforms (one as a Klingon) visit the hospital.","poster":"4d67b66325e518fae3183b8b24364994","premiere":"2010-09-19T00:00:00.0000000Z","season":2,"seasonId":"a1dd04d3de83387876e8861ed26bc69b","secs":676,"series":"Childrens Hospital","seriesId":"374db935fd4f66d27bd999d10d592bcd","tags":{"backdrop":"0f5076b938df","poster":"d665bb5444a4"},"type":"episode","year":2010},{"added":"2024-04-15T12:59:33.0000000Z","backdrop":"374db935fd4f66d27bd999d10d592bcd","ep":6,"id":"6623b7cbbf0e2d9ebd1454e94dd0bef7","mins":11,"name":"The End of the Middle","overview":"An episode of TV news magazine News Readers covering the filming of the final episode of Childrens Hospital, complete with behind the scenes looks at the show. Cutter Spindell (who portrays Blake Downs on the show within the show) interferes to save the series, convincing protesters that they're saving an actual children's hospital.","poster":"6623b7cbbf0e2d9ebd1454e94dd0bef7","premiere":"2010-09-26T00:00:00.0000000Z","season":2,"seasonId":"a1dd04d3de83387876e8861ed26bc69b","secs":